ousands separators.\n    An amount wrapped in parentheses is negative, accounting style.\n    Rows with a missing or empty amount are skipped, as are blank lines.\n    \"\"\"\n    totals = {}\n    lines = csv_text.strip().splitlines()\n    if not lines:\n        return {}\n\n    reader = csv.reader(lines)\n    try:\n        next(reader)  # Skip header\n    except StopIteration:\n        return {}\n\n    for row in reader:\n        if not row or len(row) < 3:\n            continue\n\n        category = row[1].strip().lower()\n        amount_str = row[2].strip()\n\n        if not amount_str:\n            continue\n\n        is_negative = False\n        if amount_str.startswith('(') and amount_str.endswith(')'):\n            is_negative = True\n            amount_str = amount_str[1:-1].strip()\n\n        # Remove $ and ,\n        amount_str = amount_str.replace('$', '').replace(',', '').strip()\n\n        try:\n            amount = float(amount_str)\n            if is_negative:\n                amount = -amount\n            totals[category] = totals.get(category, 0.0) + amount\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n\n    return {cat: round(amt, 2) for cat, amt in totals.items()}\n```\n\nWait, I just noticed that I might be missing some edge cases for `is_negative`.\nIf `amount_str` is `\"( $ 1,234.56 )\"`.\n`strip()` -> `\"( $ 1,234.56 )\"`\n`startswith('(')` is true. `endswith(')')` is true.\n`is_negative = True`.\n`amount_str = ' $ 1,234.56 '`.\n`amount_str.replace('$', '').replace(',', '').strip()` -> `'1234.56'`.\n`float('1234.56')` -> `1234.56`.\n`amount = -1234.56`.\nYes, it works!\n\nWhat if `amount_str` is `\"(123.45\"` (no closing parenthesis)?\n`startswith('(')` is true, but `endswith(')')` is false.\n`is_negative` remains `False`.\n`amount_str.replace('$', '').replace(',', '').strip()` -> `\"(123.45\"`.\n`float(\"(123.45\")` raises `ValueError`.\n`except ValueError: continue`.\nCorrect.\n\nWhat if `amount_str` is `\"\"` after `strip()`?\n`if not amount_str: continue` handles it.\n\nWhat if `row[1]` or `row[2]` are missing?\n`if len(row) < 3: continue` handles it.\n\nThe task is complete."}}
